'' RUN: std/fs phase P1 -- the nine error codes appended after FS_UNKNOWN and their
'' messages; WriteAtomic over the runtime's durable kernel (the caller's Rnd untouched, no
'' temporary left on success or failure, the bytes overload); MoveFile refusing an existing
'' destination with both files intact; ReplaceFile; TryExists; the "tiko" temp prefix; and a
'' long path through WriteAtomic and a long temp prefix (TS-003: a heap overflow on Linux only,
'' so the case that would have caught it is the same source run in WSL).
'' Needs the runtime of this commit (fb_UStrFsWriteAtomic, fb_UStrFsWriteAtomicText), so it
'' passes only once the toolchain is repackaged (it links the packaged libfb.a).
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/fs-p1.tiko -o tests/codegen/fsp1.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/codegen/fsp1.exe
'' RUN: tests/codegen/fsp1.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: ok
